-- Cases for the seat layer (cdba-seat.l4): every question at least once, and the not-covered answers
-- asserted. Each expected answer is worked out by hand from the text, with the working in the comment.
-- A case varies one or two answers from a baseline person: born 10 May 1990, a DTC-eligible
-- individual, resident in Canada, a citizen, return filed, no partner, no custody, no suspension,
-- asking about August 2025, adjusted income 30,000 and working income 5,000 (indexing factor 1).
-- The illustrative Consumer Price Index figure for 2024 is 100; no figure here is a published one.


§ `Seat cases`


§§ `Act s 4 and Regulations ss 2 to 2.1 -- Am I eligible?`

-- Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month (Regs s 2)?
-- The baseline person: born 10 May 1990, DTC-eligible, resident, a citizen, return filed, no partner, no custody, no suspension, asking about August 2025.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- May 2025 is not after May 2025 (s 2(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 5 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- June 2025 is the first month the criteria can be met.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Turns 18 on 2 August 2025: not 18 throughout August 2025.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 2007 8 2) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Turns 65 in August 2025: still eligible for that month (s 2(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1960 8 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Turned 65 in July 2025: not eligible for August.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1960 7 20) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- None of the five kinds of person.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A temporary resident with 18 months.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A temporary resident with only 17 months.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A partner who has not filed.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- The Minister waived the partner condition.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- In custody since June under a qualifying sentence, not released: August is neither the first month nor the month of release.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- First month of the incarceration (s 2(3)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Released on 31 August: August is the month of release.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 31) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A suspension I asked for, in force since 1 August and not resumed: suspended throughout August.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 4)
-- A suspension taking effect mid-August does not suspend payment throughout August (fork F12).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)

-- Am I at least 18 and not more than 65 years of age throughout this month (Regs s 2(1)(a))?
-- The 18th birthday falls on the first of August.
#ASSERT `Am I at least 18 and not more than 65 years of age throughout this month` (YMD 2007 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I at least 18 and not more than 65 years of age throughout this month` (YMD 2007 8 2) (YMD 2025 8 15)
-- The 65th birthday falls on the last day of August.
#ASSERT `Am I at least 18 and not more than 65 years of age throughout this month` (YMD 1960 8 31) (YMD 2025 8 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I at least 18 and not more than 65 years of age throughout this month` (YMD 1960 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15)

-- Do I turn 65 years of age in this month (Regs s 2(2))?
#ASSERT `Do I turn 65 years of age in this month` (YMD 1960 8 15) (YMD 2025 8 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Do I turn 65 years of age in this month` (YMD 1960 9 15) (YMD 2025 8 15)

-- Do my residence and status qualify me (Regs s 2(1)(c))?
-- A resident citizen.
#ASSERT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
-- A permanent resident.
#ASSERT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE
-- A protected person.
#ASSERT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE
-- An Indian under the Indian Act.
#ASSERT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 17 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Do my residence and status qualify me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 18 FALSE FALSE
-- Not resident for Income Tax Act purposes.
#ASSERT NOT `Do my residence and status qualify me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE

-- Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month (Regs s 2(1)(d))?
-- No custody.
#ASSERT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- In custody under a qualifying sentence.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- A sentence under two years does not count.
#ASSERT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- A sentence not served in a penitentiary does not count.
#ASSERT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- Released at the end of July: free in August.
#ASSERT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2025 7 31) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- A parole that was revoked is not a release: still in custody.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I free of a qualifying prison sentence this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2025 7 31) `release on parole` TRUE

-- Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released (Regs s 2(3))?
-- No custody.
#ASSERT NOT `Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 7 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- Released on the first of August.
#ASSERT `Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE
-- Released in September: August is a month in custody, not the month of release.
#ASSERT NOT `Is this the first month of my imprisonment or the month I am released` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2025 9 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE

-- Where do I stand on the condition about my spouse or partner's tax return (Regs s 2(4), 2(5))?
#ASSERT `Where do I stand on the condition about my spouse or partner's tax return` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the condition does not apply: no cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `Where do I stand on the condition about my spouse or partner's tax return` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the condition is met`
#ASSERT `Where do I stand on the condition about my spouse or partner's tax return` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the condition is not met, and the Minister has waived it`
#ASSERT `Where do I stand on the condition about my spouse or partner's tax return` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the condition is not met, and the Minister may waive it if satisfied that it is unreasonable or impracticable`

-- Is there a circumstance the Regulations name that could lead the Minister to waive the spouse or partner condition (Regs s 2(5))?
#ASSERT `Is there a circumstance named in the Regulations for a waiver` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is there a circumstance named in the Regulations for a waiver` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is there a circumstance named in the Regulations for a waiver` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- None of the three named circumstances (the Minister may still waive for other reasons: the list says "including").
#ASSERT NOT `Is there a circumstance named in the Regulations for a waiver` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- May the Minister waive the spouse or partner condition for me (Regs s 2(5))?
#ASSERT `May the Minister waive the spouse or partner condition for me` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the Minister waive the spouse or partner condition for me` FALSE

-- Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension (Regs s 2(6), 11)?
-- I asked for no suspension.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- In force from the first of August and never resumed.
#ASSERT `Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- In force from 2 August: not throughout August (fork F12).
#ASSERT NOT `Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 2) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Payment resumed in August.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 20)
-- Payment resumed only in September.
#ASSERT `Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 9 20)

-- Am I owed the supplemental amount (Regs s 2.1)?
-- An allocation paid, entitled, status resting on the certificate.
#ASSERT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- An earlier benefit payment, deemed an allocation.
#ASSERT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A payment I was not entitled to is not considered (s 2.1(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The status rests on another certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- No payment after the certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I owed the supplemental amount` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- How much is the supplemental amount (Regs s 6.1)?
#ASSERT `How much is the supplemental amount` EQUALS 150

-- How is the supplemental amount paid (Regs s 9.1)?
#ASSERT `How is the supplemental amount paid` EQUALS `paid as a lump sum`

-- Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit (Act s 4)?
-- The baseline person is eligible for the allocation.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not eligible for the allocation, and no certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not eligible for the allocation but owed the supplemental amount.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit` (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE


§§ `Regulations ss 4, 5 and 7 -- Applying, approval, and when the allocation begins`

-- On what day is my application treated as made (Regs s 4(2), 4(3))?
-- Received 1 March 2026 by a person born in 1990: the day it was received.
#ASSERT `On what day is my application treated as made` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 1990 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Not received: not made (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT `On what day is my application treated as made` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 1990 5 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Received within six months before the 18th birthday (10 May 2026): treated as received on the birthday (s 4(3)).
#ASSERT `On what day is my application treated as made` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2008 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 10)
-- Received a day before that window opens (10 November 2025): the day it was received.
#ASSERT `On what day is my application treated as made` TRUE (YMD 2025 11 9) (YMD 2008 5 10) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 11 9)

-- Do I have to make a new application (Regs s 4(4))?
-- A beneficiary who still meets the criteria of section 2.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I have to make a new application` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A beneficiary who no longer meets them (no return filed).
#ASSERT `Do I have to make a new application` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Not a beneficiary: nothing has ceased.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I have to make a new application` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Not eligible this month only because I asked for a suspension: the allocation has not ceased (fork F11).
#ASSERT NOT `Do I have to make a new application` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)

-- From what day is my application treated as approved (Regs s 5)?
-- Applied 15 September 2025; first eligible month June 2025 (1 June 2025 is later than 15 September 2023, the 24-month limit).
#ASSERT `From what day is my application treated as approved` (YMD 2025 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
-- A month more than 24 months back: no earlier than 24 months before the application (15 September 2023).
#ASSERT `From what day is my application treated as approved` (YMD 2025 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2023 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 9 15)
-- No such month: not approved.
#ASSERT `From what day is my application treated as approved` (YMD 2025 9 15) FALSE (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Which is the first month I am entitled to an allocation (Regs s 7)?
-- Approved in September 2025: the month after is October (returned as its first day).
#ASSERT `Which is the first month I am entitled to an allocation` (YMD 2025 9 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 10 1
#ASSERT `Which is the first month I am entitled to an allocation` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1


§§ `Regulations ss 6 to 9 -- How the benefit is worked out and paid`

-- Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income (Regs s 6(1), 6(4.1))?
#ASSERT `Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `subsection 6(2): no cohabiting spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `subsection 6(3): a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner who is not a beneficiary`
#ASSERT `Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `subsection 6(4): a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner who is also a beneficiary`
#ASSERT `Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `subsection 6(4.1): the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4), so subsection 6(2) applies`

-- What is my basic amount for this month, worked out under section 6 (Regs s 6(1))?
-- A single beneficiary, adjusted income 30,000, working income 5,000, August 2025 (A = 1): B = 20% x (30,000 - 5,000 - 23,000) = 400; (2,400 - 400) / 12 = 166.67.
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 166.67
-- June 2025 is in the payment period that began on 1 July 2024: no indexing factor, so not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- August 2026, with the 2024 and 2025 figures 100 and 102 (A = 1.02): B = 20% x (30,000 - 5,000 - 23,460) = 308; (2,448 - 308) / 12 = 178.33.
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2026 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 102 0 EQUALS JUST 178.33
-- Adjusted income so high that the formula goes below zero: nothing is payable (fork F9).
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 100000 0 0 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A payment period that needs the 2026 index when none is given: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2027 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 102 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A couple, both beneficiaries (A = 1): E 50,000; working incomes 10,000 + 9,000 capped at 14,000; 10% x (50,000 - 14,000 - 32,500) = 350; (2,400 - 350) / 12 = 170.83.
#ASSERT `What is my basic amount for this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 50000 10000 9000 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 170.83

-- What does the section 6 formula give for me this month, before any floor at zero (Regs s 6(1))?
#ASSERT `What does the section 6 formula give for me this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 166.67
-- The formula value, negative: (2,400 - 15,400) / 12 = -1,083.33.
#ASSERT `What does the section 6 formula give for me this month` (YMD 2025 8 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 100000 0 0 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST -1083.33
#ASSERT `What does the section 6 formula give for me this month` (YMD 2025 6 15) FALSE FALSE FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Am I entitled to an allocation for this month (Regs s 8(1))?
-- August 2025 is the first month I am entitled to, and I meet the criteria.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Asking about August when my first month is September.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- A month in which a criterion fails (no return filed).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)
-- Any day in the first month will do.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an allocation for this month` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1)

-- How much allocation is payable to me this month (Regs s 8(1))?
-- Entitled in August 2025, single, adjusted income 30,000, working income 5,000 (A = 1): 166.67.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 166.67
-- Not yet entitled: nothing is payable.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 9 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A criterion fails this month: nothing is payable.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- June 2025: no indexing factor for the payment period that began on 1 July 2024, so not covered.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2025 6 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A couple, both beneficiaries (A = 1): E 50,000, working incomes 10,000 + 9,000 capped at 14,000: 10% x (50,000 - 14,000 - 32,500) = 350; (2,400 - 350) / 12 = 170.83.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE 0 50000 10000 9000 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 170.83
-- The Minister waived the spouse condition: worked out as for a single beneficiary (s 6(4.1)): 166.67.
#ASSERT `How much allocation is payable to me this month` (YMD 2025 8 1) (YMD 2025 8 15) (YMD 1990 5 10) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) `release at the expiry of the sentence` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE 30000 0 5000 0 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 166.67

-- Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period (Regs s 8(2))?
-- 166.67 a month: paid monthly.
#ASSERT NOT `Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period` 166.67
-- Exactly 20.00: twenty dollars or less.
#ASSERT `Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period` 20
#ASSERT NOT `Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period` 20.01
-- Nothing payable: s 8(2) does not engage (fork F10).
#ASSERT NOT `Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period` 0

-- How big would my lump sum for the payment period be (Regs s 8(2))?
-- 15.00 a month from July: 12 months remaining.
#ASSERT `How big would my lump sum for the payment period be` 15 (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 9 1) EQUALS 180
-- From November: November to June is 8 months.
#ASSERT `How big would my lump sum for the payment period be` 15 (YMD 2025 11 20) (YMD 2025 11 20) EQUALS 120

-- What will my first payment of the allocation be (Regs s 9)?
-- October, November and December 2025: three months of 166.67.
#ASSERT `What will my first payment of the allocation be` (YMD 2025 9 15) (YMD 2025 12 20) 166.67 EQUALS JUST 500.01
-- The first payment in the month of approval: no months in the period; not covered.
#ASSERT `What will my first payment of the allocation be` (YMD 2025 9 15) (YMD 2025 9 30) 166.67 EQUALS NOTHING


§§ `Regulations ss 10 and 11 -- Suspension of payments`

-- Can the Minister suspend my payments (Regs s 10(1))?
#ASSERT `Can the Minister suspend my payments` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Minister suspend my payments` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister suspend my payments` FALSE FALSE

-- Can the Minister keep my payments suspended (Regs s 10(1))?
-- Not yet satisfied: the suspension may continue.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister keep my payments suspended` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister keep my payments suspended` TRUE

-- Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility (Regs s 10(2))?
#ASSERT `Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility` FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- Must the Minister resume my payments and pay me what I missed (Regs s 10(3))?
#ASSERT `Must the Minister resume my payments and pay me what I missed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister resume my payments and pay me what I missed` FALSE

-- How much will I be paid when the Minister lifts a suspension (Regs s 10(3))?
-- Three months of 166.67.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid when the Minister lifts a suspension` 166.67 3 EQUALS 500.01
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid when the Minister lifts a suspension` 166.67 0 EQUALS 0

-- On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them (Regs s 11(1), 11(2))?
-- No day named: the last day of the month in which the request is processed.
#ASSERT `On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them` TRUE (YMD 2025 8 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 9 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 8 31)
-- A later day named: that day.
#ASSERT `On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them` TRUE (YMD 2025 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 9 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 9 15)
-- An earlier day named: the last day of the processing month is later.
#ASSERT `On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them` TRUE (YMD 2025 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 8 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 8 31)
-- Not in writing: not a request under s 11(1).
#ASSERT `On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them` FALSE (YMD 2025 8 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 9 15) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is my request to resume payments in time (Regs s 11(3))?
-- Received on the last day of the 24 months.
#ASSERT `Is my request to resume payments in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2027 8 31) TRUE
-- A day late.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my request to resume payments in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2027 9 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my request to resume payments in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) (YMD 2027 8 31) FALSE

-- Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time (Regs s 11(3))?
-- No request in time and the 24 months are over.
#ASSERT `Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2027 9 1)
-- The 24 months have not yet run out.
#ASSERT NOT `Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2027 8 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time` (YMD 2025 8 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 1 5) (YMD 2027 9 1)

-- Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask (Regs s 11(4))?
#ASSERT `Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask` FALSE TRUE

-- In which month will my payments resume (Regs s 11(5))?
-- The month after the request was received (returned as its first day).
#ASSERT `In which month will my payments resume` (YMD 2025 10 10) FALSE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS YMD 2025 11 1
-- A later month named.
#ASSERT `In which month will my payments resume` (YMD 2025 10 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 12 20) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 1
-- An earlier month named: the month after receipt is later.
#ASSERT `In which month will my payments resume` (YMD 2025 10 10) TRUE (YMD 2025 9 3) EQUALS YMD 2025 11 1


§§ `Regulations ss 12 to 16 -- Death of a beneficiary, and representatives`

-- Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died (Regs s 12)?
-- An heir.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` TRUE `heir`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` TRUE `executor or administrator of the estate`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` TRUE `liquidator of the succession`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` TRUE `none of these`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` FALSE `heir`

-- Can the estate or the heirs claim the allocation for the month the beneficiary died (Regs s 13(1))?
#ASSERT `Can the estate or the heirs claim the allocation for the month of death` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the estate or the heirs claim the allocation for the month of death` TRUE TRUE

-- Who is paid an amount owing when a beneficiary dies (Regs s 13(2))?
#ASSERT `Who is paid an amount owing when a beneficiary dies` TRUE EQUALS `the beneficiary's estate or succession or the beneficiary's heirs`
#ASSERT `Who is paid an amount owing when a beneficiary dies` FALSE EQUALS `a person or agency designated by the Minister`

-- Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared (Regs s 14(1))?
#ASSERT `Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared` FALSE TRUE

-- Will I be paid if the Minister changes the date of a presumed death or finds the beneficiary alive (Regs s 14(2), 14(3))?
#ASSERT `Will the benefit be paid if the Minister changes the presumed date of death or finds me alive` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the benefit be paid if the Minister changes the presumed date of death or finds me alive` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Will the benefit be paid if the Minister changes the presumed date of death or finds me alive` FALSE FALSE

-- May my representative act for me (Regs s 15)?
#ASSERT `May my representative act for me` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May my representative act for me` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May my representative act for me` TRUE FALSE

-- May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative (Regs s 16)?
#ASSERT `May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative` FALSE TRUE


§§ `Regulations ss 17 to 19 and 31 -- Challenging a decision, and more time`

-- Can the Minister change a decision made about me (Regs s 17)?
#ASSERT `Can the Minister change a decision made about me` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister change a decision made about me` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can the Minister change a decision made about me` FALSE TRUE

-- Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision (Regs s 18(1), 18(2))?
-- No benefit paid.
#ASSERT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive` TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35` TRUE
-- A decision on reconsideration is appealed, not reconsidered again.
#ASSERT NOT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `any other decision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` FALSE

-- By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision (Regs s 18(1), 18(2))?
-- Notified 1 January 2026: 180 days later is 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 30
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision` (YMD 2025 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27

-- Is my request for reconsideration in time (Regs s 18, 19)?
-- Made on the last day of the 180 days.
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my request for reconsideration in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15)
-- Made on the last day the Minister extended it to.
#ASSERT `Is my request for reconsideration in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 9 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my request for reconsideration in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 9 16) TRUE (YMD 2026 9 15)

-- Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require (Regs s 18(3))?
#ASSERT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Incapable, and the representative's details are missing.
#ASSERT NOT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons (Regs s 18(4))?
-- A proper request, in time, about a decision of no benefit.
#ASSERT `Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- A day late and no extension.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons` `any other decision` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- By what day must I ask the Minister for more time (Regs s 19(1))?
-- Notified 1 January 2026: the 180 days end 30 June 2026; 185 days after that is 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask the Minister for more time` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1

-- Must the Minister allow me more time (Regs s 19(3))?
#ASSERT `Must the Minister allow me more time` `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire` TRUE
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister allow me more time` `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister allow me more time` `none of these` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister allow me more time` `an emotional or mental distress suffered by the person, such as from a death in their family` TRUE

-- Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason (Regs s 19(2), 19(4))?
#ASSERT `Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 1) FALSE

-- Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit (Regs s 31)?
#ASSERT `Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE


§§ `Act s 10.1 and Regulations ss 20 to 29 -- Appeals`

-- Does the Act let me appeal this decision (Act s 10.1)?
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me appeal this decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me appeal this decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me appeal this decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act let me appeal this decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- How can I challenge this decision (Regs s 20)?
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` EQUALS `ask the Minister to reconsider it under section 18`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` EQUALS `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
#ASSERT `How can I challenge this decision` `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)` EQUALS `appeal it to the Social Security Tribunal`
-- Not covered: the text states no route.
